<title>INDIA: India 96/97 lead output drops to 43,780 tonnes.</title>
<headline>India 96/97 lead output drops to 43,780 tonnes.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 43,780 tonnes of lead in 1996/97 (April-March), down from 45,655 tonnes in the previous fiscal year, the Mines Ministry said on Monday.  </p>
<p>The ministry said in a statement that the country produced 4,965 tonnes of lead in March against a target of 5,315 tonnes.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	   Installed  March, 1997	 Cumulative output</p>
<p>	   capacity   -----------	 -----------------</p>
<p>	   (annual)     Actual	Apr 96-Mar 97  Apr 95-Mar 96</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>HZL	 65,000	3,740	    27,874	   27,843</p>
<p>ILL</p>
<p>Secondary 24,000	1,225	    15,906	   17,812</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>Total     89,000	4,965	    43,780	   45,655</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes and provisional.</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91-11 301 2024</p>
